A RESOLUTION TO ESTABLISH SIGN PERMIT FEES FOR THE CONSTRUCTION, ERECTION, AND CREATION OF SIGNS WITHIN THE TOWN OF CLERMONT, GEORGIA, AND TO PUBLISH THE PERMIT FEE SCHEDULE; TO PROVIDE FOR AN EFFECTIVE DATE; AND FOR OTHER PURPOSES.

WHEREAS, the Town Council of the Town of Clermont, Georgia is authorized by O. C. G. A. § 36-66-1 and the Town Charter, to exercise its police power to enact zoning ordinances to provide regulations as to land use as to property within the Town of Clermont, Georgia; and

WHEREAS, the Town Council has enacted a sign ordinance that regulates the use of signs upon property within the Town of Clermont, Georgia;

WHEREAS, Section 6.2 of the Sign Ordinance of the Town of Clermont provides that the Town Council may establish sign permit fees by resolution duly passed by the Town Council of the Town of Clermont, Georgia;

WHEREAS, the Town Council finds that it is in the best interest of the Town, for the Town Council to set sign permit fees for the construction, erection, and creation of signs within the Town of Clermont, Georgia.

NOW, THEREFORE, BE IT RESOLVED, by the Town Council of Clermont, Georgia and it is hereby resolved by the authority of the Town Charter and the above-referenced authority, as amended:
